# ─── C ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
c: "C. THE COMPILER  ::  one .dl6 in, one TS module out" {
  class: stage
  direction: down

  src: |`prolog
  rel orchard.tree(tree_id: int, species: text).
  orchard.fruit(TreeId, Picked) <- orchard.tree(TreeId, _), harvest(TreeId, Picked).
  `| { shape: document; class: src }

  text_door: "TEXT DOOR  ::  compile/parse_dl.pl:1062 head_atom\n\nno dot route. `a.b(X) <- c(X).` is dl_parse_error(statement, position(1,2))" {
    shape: parallelogram
    class: danger
    link: "${src}/v6/prolog/compile/parse_dl.pl#1062"
  }

  term: "prog(Decls, Rules)  ::  the retained program term" {
    shape: stored_data
    class: shipped
  }

  expand: "1_expansion.pl  ::  the phase driver, expansion_phase/3" {
    grid-rows: 1
    grid-columns: 2
    grid-gap: 16
    class: designed

    phases: |||md
    | order | phase | expander |
    |---|---|---|
    | 10 | `enum` | `enum_expand:expand_enum_in_context` |
    | 20 | `decl_spread` | **unwired** |
    | 30 | `row_spread` | **unwired** |
    | 40 | `match` | `match_expand:...` |
    | 42 | `seq` | `seq_expand:...` |
    | 44 | `dot` | `dot_expand:...` |
    | 45 | `coalesce` | `coalesce_expand:...` |
    | 46 | `ast` | `ast_expand:...` |
    | 50 | `relation_edge` | `relation_edge_expand:...` |

    Order is the number, so no arrow is needed. Two slots are declared and
    unwired, which is why the table beats a chain of boxes.
    ||| { class: shipped; shape: rectangle }

    notes: |||md
    ## the two that matter to the module arc
    **10 enum** is the shipped answer to nesting on the right-hand side:
    `:176` joins the name, `:107` mints `body_tag`, `:89-98` THROWS on a clash,
    and `:12-16` keeps `enum_context/2` because expansion erases its own input.

    **44 dot** is where the module half is missing. `0_dot_expand.pl:29` says
    "There is no module half in scope", and a dotted head silently becomes a rel
    named `dot_get`.

    Phase 10 already does, for values, what phase 44 must learn to do for names.
    ||| { class: danger; shape: rectangle }
  }

  analyze: "analyze.pl  ::  level graph, recursiveHeads/2, program_uses_catalog at :190" {
    shape: hexagon
    class: shipped
    link: "${src}/v6/prolog/analyze.pl#191"
