# ─── D ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
d: "D. THE SYMMETRY  ::  two intern tables, one mechanism" {
  class: stage
  grid-rows: 2
  grid-columns: 2
  grid-gap: 20

  typeside: "TYPE side, shipped" {
    class: shipped
    direction: down

    dictbox: "a declared type lowers to this" {
      tbl: "file" {
        shape: sql_table
        __id: "INTEGER PRIMARY KEY -- the interned id" { constraint: PK }
        repo: "TEXT NOT NULL"
        at: "INTEGER NOT NULL -- an fpath __id" { constraint: FK }
        __refcount: "INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1"
        u: "UNIQUE (repo, at) -- the hash-cons" { constraint: UNQ }
      }
    }
    view: "__ref_file\n\nTEMP VIEW, dies with the connection.\nEvery join is parent.col = child.__id" {
      shape: page
      class: muted
    }
  }

  relside: "REL side, building" {
    class: designed
    direction: down

    relbox: "__rel, renamed from __catalog_rel at h1" {
      tbl: "__rel" {
        shape: sql_table
        rel_id: "INTEGER PRIMARY KEY -- the interned id" { constraint: PK }
        parent_id: "INT -- who contains me" { constraint: FK }
        ordinal: "INT -- 0 on a rel, 1-based on a column"
        local_name: "TEXT -- last segment only"
        kind: "TEXT -- primitive|rel|column|module|instance"
        type_id: "INT -- what I am" { constraint: FK }
        arity: "INT -- h2, closes the table_name drop"
        module_id: "INT -- h4, which file I came from" { constraint: FK }
        h_id: "BLOB -- h4, stable across recompiles" { constraint: UNQ }
        h_schema: "BLOB -- h5, drives DROP"
        h_rule: "BLOB -- h5, drives recompute"
        h_rows: "BLOB -- h6, drives propagation"
        refcount: "INT -- how many rules name me"
        u: "UNIQUE (parent_id, local_name, arity)" { constraint: UNQ }
      }
    }
    receipt: |`sql
    -- g1 receipt, already true:
    EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN
      SELECT rel_id, local_name FROM "__rel" WHERE parent_id = ?;
    -- SEARCH __rel USING COVERING INDEX __rel_parent
    `| { class: muted }
  }

  claim: |||md
  ## the whole claim
  A **type** interns VALUES keyed by a column tuple.
  A **rel** interns NAMES keyed by `(parent_id, local_name, arity)`.

  | | type side | rel side |
  |---|---|---|
  | hash-cons | `UNIQUE (cols)` | `UNIQUE (parent, name, arity)` |
  | the id | `__id` rowid | `rel_id` rowid |
  | liveness | `__refcount` -> 0, row dies | `refcount` -> 0, table dies |
  | on collision | THROW, shipped | THROW, not built |

  The rel side needs ONE thing the type side never did: a per-file
  disambiguator. Two FILES can carry one rel name; two variants in one
  file cannot.
  ||| { class: chosen; shape: rectangle }
}

# ─── F ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
f: "F. FOUR HASHES  ::  each breaks exactly one thing" {
  class: stage
  grid-rows: 2
  grid-columns: 2
  grid-gap: 20

  ladder: |latex
  \begin{aligned}
  h_{id}     &= H(\text{module\_id},\ \text{local\_name},\ \text{arity}) \\
  h_{schema} &= H(\text{columns},\ \text{types},\ \text{key}) \\
  h_{rule}   &= H(\text{canonical rule bodies for this head}) \\
  h_{rows}   &= H(\text{the rows})
  \end{aligned}
  | { class: chosen; shape: rectangle }

  blast: "blast radius, strictly decreasing" {
    direction: down
    hid: "h_id differs\n\nA DIFFERENT REL.\nNothing is reused." { class: muted }
    hs: "h_schema differs\n\nDROP + CREATE.\nRows lost, on purpose." { class: danger }
    hr: "h_rule differs\n\nKeep the table.\nDELETE + recompute." { class: chosen }
    hw: "h_rows differs\n\nWake the consumers.\nEQUAL: red stops here." { class: shipped }
    hid -> hs -> hr -> hw: "less damage each rung" { style.stroke: "#5f6368" }
  }

  trap: |||md
  ## the one way to get it wrong
  Put `h_schema` in the NAME, and one added column renames the table:

  `orchard__tree__f9fc8ea9` -> `orchard__tree__3b1c02aa`

  A rename in SQLite is a **new empty table**. The old rows sit in a name
  nothing will ever ask for again.

  | level | Rust hashes it? |
  |---|---|
  | crate root | **yes**, `StableCrateId` = H(name, `-C metadata`) |
  | module path segment | no, `7mycrate7example` |
  | item body / columns | **never** |

  So the hash is a COLUMN of `__rel`, and the name stays boring.
  ||| { class: danger; shape: rectangle }

  verdicts: |||md
  ## the five verdicts, which are just those hashes read in order
  | verdict | test | DDL | rows | consumers |
  |---|---|---|---|---|
  | **NEW** | `h_id` misses | `CREATE` | seeded | RED |
  | **RESHAPED** | `h_schema` differs | `DROP` + `CREATE` | **LOST** | RED |
  | **REBODIED** | `h_rule` differs | none | `DELETE` + recompute | check `h_rows` |
  | **GREEN** | all four equal | none | untouched | **nobody wakes** |
  | **GONE** | absent from the new compile | `DROP` | dropped | RED |

  GREEN is the one that pays for the other four.
  ||| { class: shipped; shape: rectangle }
}

# ─── G ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
gh: "G. PRIOR ART, AND WHAT IS STILL OPEN" {
  class: stage
  grid-rows: 3
  grid-columns: 2
  grid-gap: 20

  table: |||md
  | system | unit | id INSIDE | name at the EXIT | on collision |
  |---|---|---|---|---|
  | **Rust** | crate | `DefId = (CrateNum, DefIndex)` | `_RNvCs7qp2U7fqm6G_7mycrate7example` | crate-level hash IN the symbol, never the body |
  | **Go** | package (a dir) | `Sym = (Pkg, Name)`, "a segmented namespace" | `import/path.Name`, bad bytes `%`-escaped | a compile error, no hash anywhere |
  | **Python** | file or dir | `sys.modules["a.b.c"]` + attr on the parent | the dotted string itself | parent first, one lock per name |
  | **SQLite** | attached db | `(schema, table)` | `other.t` | none needed, both live, `MAX_ATTACHED=10` |
  | **dl v5** | none | none | the bare rel name | **last writer wins, silently** |

  Two of the five refuse on collision. Zero of the five hash content into a name.
  ||| { class: shipped; shape: rectangle }

  quote: |||md
  ## the sentence that settles it
  From Go's own source, `cmd/compile/internal/types/sym.go:14`:

  > Sym represents an object name in a **segmented** (pkg, name) namespace.

  Segmented. Two parts. Joined only at the linker, and escaped rather than
  hashed when joined. Your `__rel.parent_id` + `local_name` IS that pair;
  `orchard__tree` is the linker step.
  ||| { class: chosen; shape: rectangle }

  grid-rows: 2
  grid-columns: 2
  grid-gap: 20

  user: "needs your word" {
    class: chosen
    u1: "hash function:\nxxh3, or truncated SHA-256?" { shape: hexagon; class: chosen }
    u2: "module separator: __\nso orchard__tree never reads\nlike the enum join body_page" { shape: hexagon; class: chosen }
    u3: "a RESHAPE deletes rows under a\nrunning server. silently, or refuse\nand demand a flag?" { shape: hexagon; class: chosen }
  }

  ready: "dispatchable now" {
    class: shipped
    d1: "h1  rename __catalog_rel -> __rel" { shape: step; class: shipped }
    d2: "h2  arity into table_name/2" { shape: step; class: shipped }
  }

  chain: "chained, and on what" {
    class: designed
    b1: "h3  dotted name through the parser\nblocked on NOTHING. this is the unblocker." { shape: step; class: designed }
    b2: "h4  module_id + h_id" { shape: step; class: muted }
    b3: "h5  the five-verdict swap" { shape: step; class: muted }
    b4: "h6  h_rows red/green propagation" { shape: step; class: muted }
    b1 -> b2 -> b3 -> b4: "strict order" { style.stroke: "#5f6368" }
  }

  carried: |||md
  ## carried, older than today
  | item | state |
  |---|---|
  | dotted-head fork, A or B | unfalsifiable until multi-file compile exists |
  | primitives: reserved ids 1..5, or looked up at seed? | open since 2026-08-05 |
  | does the HTTP door learn `__rel`? | open since 2026-08-05 |
  | 35 worktrees | `git worktree remove` is classifier-blocked, you run it |
  | **push** | 7 commits, no tag, gate green |
  ||| { class: muted; shape: rectangle }
}
